      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00020:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "Lewis structure of dimethyl sulfoxide with breakdown of valence, bonding, and nonbonding electrons. Sulfur owns five electrons in structure, formal positive. Oxygen owns seven electrons in structure, formal negative."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_02_03_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
